In article <824@quirm.terminus.ericsson.se>, I wrote:

|> 2) xtb (and rtb) fail on machines with hostnames >15 chars (spotted by
|> jacob@cs.washington.edu)
|> 

The fix I gave in the previous article, doesn't fix the problem. The solution
is to increase the value of HOSTLEN on line 34 up in defs.h to a value large
enough to hold the longest of the hostnames (for example 32). (As pointed
out to be by jacob@cs.washington.edu and sheldon@iastate.edu). This has
two side effects, the network bandwith used by the game is increased, and
you would be unable to play against someone else with a different value
for HOSTLEN.

This is only a short term solution, I shall work on a better bug fix.

